course: dictionary
lesson: 15610
title: Tardy: late, slow, or a school mark
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tardy means late, arriving after the right time. «Don't be tardy for class.» The word class tells you that you should be there on time, so tardy means not on time.
explain: Tardy can also mean slow to act or happen. «He was tardy in replying to my letter, and it took two weeks.» Two weeks is a long time, so tardy here means slow.
explain: In US and Canadian schools, tardy is everyday school language. «The tardy bell rang, and the last children ran into the hall.» In the UK and Australia, people usually say late instead.
fact: Tardy means late, arriving after the right time.
fact: «Tardy» can also mean slow to act or happen.
fact: In US and Canadian schools, «a tardy» is a mark against you for arriving late.
fact: A «tardy slip» and a «tardy bell» are school words you may hear in the US.
fact: In the UK and Australia, people mostly say «late» where Americans say «tardy».
exercise: «Don't be tardy for class.» What does tardy mean? | Tired | *Late | Early | Happy
exercise: «The tardy bell rang, and the last children ran into the hall.» What is the tardy bell? | A bell that means a fire drill | *The school bell that rings to start class | A church bell | A bell for lunch
exercise: «He was tardy in replying to my letter.» What does tardy suggest? | Rude about the letter | Very fast | *Slow to act | Very kind
test: Which word means the same as tardy? | Quick | *Late | Loud | Early
test: «I got three tardies this month.» In a US school, what is a tardy? | Lunch money | A bus stop | *A mark for arriving late | A school trip
exam: Which word fits the gap? «The train was ___, so we missed the start of the match.» | Early | Quiet | *Tardy | Happy
